# No personal paths or identity in the repo

The user may paste a local absolute path in chat so you can find a file. Treat that as **private working context only**.

Never copy it into README, comments, tests, commit messages, PR titles/bodies, screenshots, or other committed files.

## Do not write

- Windows home paths: `C:\Users\<name>\...` or `C:/Users/<name>/...`
- macOS home paths: `/Users/<name>/...`
- Real usernames, emails, phone numbers, or machine hostnames
- Other secrets: tokens, passwords, API keys, cookies

## Write instead

- Generic examples: `input.pdf`, `document.pdf`, `selected.pdf`
- Placeholders: `C:\Users\<you>\Documents\file.pdf`, `~/Documents/file.pdf`
- Repo-relative paths that already exist in this project

If a prompt contains a personal path, use it to locate or copy the file if needed, then document the public/generic name only.
